Assembler Version 07
====================
Assembled by: version 06 (instgen assembled by v06, asm assembled by v06)

Features Supported by This Assembler
-------------------------------------
Same non-standard mnemonic syntax as version 06, with flag-based instruction
encoding and additional instructions:

Syntax:
- Non-standard (custom) mnemonic syntax: LDA#, LDAZ, STAZ, etc.
- DATA pseudo-instruction for raw byte emission
- Hex constants: $xx (1 byte) or $xxxx (2 bytes)
- Quoted strings with \n escape
- Label definitions with PC value or explicit assignment
- PC setting via: * = $xxxx
- Low byte (<) and high byte (>) operators on labels
- Relative branch (~label) syntax
- Labels as 2-byte operands
- Comments with semicolons
- Two-pass assembly
- Flag-based operand type detection (INST_RELATIVE, INST_BYTE, INST_PSUEDO)

Instruction set (non-standard mnemonics, expanded from v06):
- ADC#, ADCZ, AND#, ASLA
- BCC, BCS, BEQ, BITZ, BMI, BNE, BPL, BRK
- CLC, CMPZ, CMP#, CMP,Y, CPY#
- DECZ, DEX
- EORZ
- INCZ, INX, INY
- JMP, JSR
- LDA, LDX, LDY (absolute), LDA#, LDAZ(),Y, LDA,X, LDA,Y, LDAZ, LDAZ,X, LDX#, LDY#
- LSRA
- ORAZ
- PHA, PLA
- ROLZ, RTS
- SBC#, SBCZ, SEC
- STA, STAZ(),Y, STA,X, STA,Y, STAZ, STAZ,X
- TAX, TAY, TSX, TXA, TYA

Error handling:
- Label not found (error 1)
- Duplicate label (error 2)
- Opcode not found (error 3)
- Expected hex value (error 4)
- Branch out of range (error 5)

New in this version (relative to version 06):
- Instruction table generator (instgen.asm) - generates pre-computed instruction
  hash table as assembly source, which is prepended to the assembler source
- Flag-based instruction encoding: each instruction has a flags byte encoding
  whether the operand is relative ($02), a single byte ($04), or pseudo ($01)
- Automatic operand type selection based on instruction flags (no longer relies
  solely on explicit ~ prefix for relative branches)
- Branch out of range error detection with validation
- New instructions: CMPZ, CPY#, DECZ, DEX, LDA/LDX/LDY (absolute), ROLZ,
  TAX, TSX, TXA
- 128-entry hash tables (reduced from 256)
- read_b renamed from read (to distinguish from environment read)

Features Used in This Assembler's Source Code
----------------------------------------------
- Non-standard mnemonic syntax (LDA#, LDAZ, STAZ, etc.)
- DATA pseudo-instruction
- Hex constants ($xx and $xxxx)
- Quoted strings with escape sequences
- Labels and label assignments
- PC setting (* = $2000, set in instgen output)
- Low byte (<) and high byte (>) operators
- Relative branch (~label) syntax
- Two-byte label operands
- Comments (;)
- BRK with inline error code and message
- Prepended instruction hash table (generated by instgen.asm)

New syntax used in source (relative to version 06):
- None

Other source changes:
- Source is split into two files: instgen.asm (generates instruction table)
  and asm.asm (the assembler itself, with inst.asm prepended)
- Instruction hash table loaded from generated code rather than built at runtime
